cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference Tzun in academic or policy work, please cite it as below."
title: "Tzun: cryptographic evidence capture for AI decisions"
abstract: >-
  Tzun records a tamper-evident Decision Evidence Object when a human acts on an
  AI recommendation: canonical serialization, SHA-256 digest, an append-only hash
  chain, and optional WebAuthn signatures, RFC 3161 timestamps and an AI Bill of
  Materials describing the model that produced the recommendation.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tzun, Inc."
    website: "https://tzun.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TzunAI/tzun"
url: "https://tzun.ai"
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - AI accountability
  - human-in-the-loop
  - tamper-evident logging
  - hash chain
  - RFC 3161
  - AI bill of materials
  - audit evidence
  - EU AI Act
